   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to approvals, notices and consents to certificates of incorporation",
    "basePrintNo": "S7198",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7198-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §404, N-PC L",
    "lawSection": "Not-for-Profit Corporation Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7198\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the not-for-profit corporation law, in relation to\napprovals, notices and consents to certificates of incorporation\n\n PURPOSE OF THE BILL :\n\nTo amend Section 404(i) of the Not-For-Profit Law relating to\napprovals, notices and consents to certificates of incorporation for\nnot-for-profit corporations that solicit funds for or otherwise\nbenefit the Armed Forces of the United State or of any foreign country\nor their auxiliaries.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend Section 404, paragraph (i) of the\nNot-For-Profit Corporation (NFPC) Law, in relation to the requirement\nfor endorsement by the \"Chief of Staff\" of every certificate of\nincorporation which seeks to solicit funds for or otherwise benefit\nthe Armed Forces of the United States or of any foreign country or\ntheir auxiliaries. This sections deletes the words \"Chief of Staff\"\nand inserts the words \"Adjutant General\".\n\nSection 2 of the bill would provide an immediate effective date.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nSection 404, paragraph (i), formerly paragraph (h), was amended by\nChapter 1058, Section 9, of the Laws of 1971; previously paragraph\n(i), was amended by Chapter 141, Section 72 of the Laws of 1988; so\ndesignated paragraph (h) by Chapter 139, section 1 of the Laws of\n1993; and so designated paragraph (i), amended by Chapter 431, Section\n1, of the Laws of 1993, deemed effective August 30, 1993.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThis bill would amend the NFPC law relating to the requirement for\nendorsement by the \"Chief of Staff' of every certificate of\nincorporation which seeks to solicit funds for or otherwise benefit\nthe Armed Forces of the United States or of any foreign country or\ntheir auxiliaries.\n\nIn 1988, the title of the commissioner of DMNA was changed in the\nMilitary Law from \"Chief of Staff' to \"the Adjutant General.\" As a\nresult, individuals seeking to incorporate a NFP organization related\nto the Armed Forces have experienced some confusion as to which state\nofficial is the endorsing authority. This bill will eliminate\nconfusion and delay by clearly identifying the Adjutant General as the\nendorsing authority for a certificate of incorporation that is pending\napproval before the Department of State.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediate.\n",
